        "check": "Root D34: `composer lint:check`, `composer analyse`, `composer test`, `composer test:pg`; `composer test:arch`, contract guard and anti-weakening gate; affected `composer --working-dir=packages/tenancy test` / analyse. For any src delta `bash scripts/mutation-check.sh --all` (D98). Before tests prove test-isolation/preflight, PG _test only; default package test may include PG. Core storage tests per-package and included root harness. No floors weakened. Required receipt envelope and meaningful invariants below; new source inputs rerun affected proofs. All Filesystem methods (null directories, batch delete, from/to, stream writes, visibility, path/url), encoded traversal/backslash/NUL/absolute paths/symlink deny; A→B/root/no context old handles deny, no rebind of cached disk. Existing opened stream cannot be magically revoked: scope access at acquisition, stream consumed/closed within owning context; prevent publication/use across lifecycle by composition and explicit boundary receipt. Two real isolated DBs A/B and root have distinguishing sentinel rows; success/exception/retry/nested run restore/reset connection+workspace. Local/fake-S3/native-SDK service evidence distinguished; native provider outage no fallback to wrong tenant. Archive/lab consumer cases. Read-only `python3 plans/2026.09.15-№1-COREX-FLEXCRM-REMAINING/scripts/validate-p3.py --stage branches --report findings/P3-storage-context.md`; Report ## Cases/Inputs/Adoption schemas and all local required cases PASS; every effective pending condition retains owner/resume.",
